import collections,json
from pathlib import Path
out=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
read=lambda n:json.loads((out/n).read_text())
p=read('provenance.json');groups=read('grouped-first-stops.json');comparison=read('comparison.json');art=read('root-order.json');totals=read('latent-totals.json');excerpts=read('source-excerpts.json')
checks={r['root']:r for r in art['checks']}
q=lambda x:'`'+str(x)+'`'
lines=['# Next stops on main f1c19c6a','','Measured for tasks baobab and b5w3ycg. Report only.','',f'Compiler and apply SHA: {q(p["sha"])}. TypeScript 6.0.3 source pin: {q(p["typescript_pin"])}.','',f'Box: {q(p["box"])}; {p["cpus"]} visible CPUs; CPU quota {q(p["cpu_max"])}; {p["meminfo"]}. Started {p["date"]}.','','## Grouped first stops','','Locations and root names are relative to src/compiler/. Only the first observation counts. Duplicate observations agree in all non-timing fields.','','| Roots | Location | Kind | Exact reason | Compared with 7910ab94 | Root names |','| ---: | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |']
for g in groups:
 names=', '.join(q(r)+(' ('+checks[r]['classification']+')' if r in checks else '') for r in g['roots'])
 lines.append(f'| {g["count"]} | {q(g["where"])} | {g["kind"]} | '+g['reason'].replace('|','\\|')+f' | '+(', '.join(str(g[k])+' '+k for k in ['unchanged','moved','new'] if g[k])+f' | {names} |'))
accepted=[r for g in groups if g['kind']=='accepted' for r in g['roots']]
lines+=['','The table records measured first stops. Exact per-root changes follow below.','','## Roots lowering whole','',f'{len(accepted)}/79: '+', '.join(map(q,accepted))+'. Lower acceptance covers each complete resolved root program. Native output is not measured.','','## Comparison with 7910ab94','','Baseline: 7910ab94a42b0c7f62a79329d7f250b1b2045d05, from typescript/next-stops-7910ab94. Its report and grouped data are retained in previous-REPORT.md and previous-grouped-first-stops.json. Unchanged means an identical (location, kind, exact reason) tuple for that root. Moved means a different tuple present in the baseline. New means a tuple absent from the baseline.','','| Current group | Roots | Unchanged | Moved | New |','| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |']
for g in groups:
 c=collections.Counter(r['classification'] for r in comparison if r['root'] in g['roots'])
 lines.append(f'| {q(g["where"])} {g["kind"]} | {g["count"]} | {c["unchanged"]} | {c["moved"]} | {c["new"]} |')
c=collections.Counter(r['classification'] for r in comparison)
lines+=['',f'Total: {c["unchanged"]} unchanged, {c["moved"]} moved, {c["new"]} new. Exact before and after reasons are in comparison.json.','','| Root | Classification | Before location / kind | After location / kind |','| --- | --- | --- | --- |']
for r in comparison:lines.append(f'| {q(r["root"])} | {r["classification"]} | {q(r["before"][0])} {r["before"][1]} | {q(r["after"][0])} {r["after"][1]} |')
emitters={"a namespace object used as a value; no runtime container is emitted, so identity, receiver behavior, live export aliases and staged properties are not represented; use qualified members or named module imports":'internal/lower/namespaces.go:233 emits this NotYet reason.', "a cast the runtime can't check":'internal/lower/cast_proof.go:195 (castRefusal).', 'reading an enum before its runtime initialization; move the call after the enum declaration':'internal/lower/namespaces.go:267 and :318 emit this NotYet reason.', 'a namespace read before runtime initialization, directly or through a reachable call; move that read or call after the namespace declaration':'internal/lower/namespaces.go:269 and :321 emit this NotYet reason.'}
lines+=['','## Stop source and lowering emitters','']
for g in groups:
 if g['where']=='-':continue
 e=next(e for e in excerpts if e['where']==g['where'])
 lines += [f'### {g["where"]}','',g['kind']+': '+q(g['reason'])+'. '+emitters.get(g['reason'], 'See lowering-emitter-excerpts.txt for exact emitting lines.'),'','```ts',e['text'].rstrip(),'```','']
for name in ['debug','semver']:
 findings=read(name+'-full-findings.json'); status=read(name+'-full-status.json')
 lines += ['## '+name+'.ts single-file full-mode census','', 'LATENT_FULL=1, LATENT_ASSERT_NO_OUTPUT=1, LATENT_ONLY_FILE set to the exact adapted src/compiler/'+name+'.ts path. The meter latent binary loaded the complete compiler directory. Child exit '+str(status['exit_code'])+'; elapsed '+format(status['seconds'],'.3f')+' seconds. Findings below are in source order; all kinds and phases are retained.','', '| Phase | Kind | Location | Exact reason |','| --- | --- | --- | --- |']
 for f in findings:
  lines.append('| '+f.get('phase','')+' | '+f.get('kind','')+' | '+q(f.get('where','').split('/src/compiler/')[-1])+' | '+f.get('reason','').replace('|','\\|').replace('\n','<br>')+' |')
 lines += ['']
lines+=['## Root-order evidence','',f'Classification: {art["status"]}. '+(art.get('stopping_reason') or 'The entry per-source ledger completed.'),'','The baseline report.py criteria require attempted-source and readiness-finding evidence from the entry run plus a Node throw. An incomplete entry ledger cannot establish an artifact. Independent stops remain counted.','','| Root | Independent stop | Node exit | First error | Label |','| --- | --- | ---: | --- | --- |']
for r in art['checks']:lines.append(f'| {q(r["root"])} | {q(r["where"])} | {r["node"]["exit"]} | {r["node"]["first_error"]} | {r["classification"]} |')
e=totals['guarded_entry'];s=e['child_status'];c=e['finding_totals'];o=totals['ordinary_counted_observations']['first_stop_totals']
lines+=['','## Latent totals','',f'Guarded entry: LATENT_FULL=1, LATENT_ASSERT_NO_OUTPUT=1, bound 1800 seconds. Child exit {s["exit_code"]}; elapsed {s["seconds"]:.3f} seconds; stopping reason {s["stopping_reason"] or "completed"}. Emitted findings: NotYet {c["NotYet"]}, Refused {c["Refused"]}, panics {c["panic"]}. Completed sources {e["completed_sources"]}/{e["expected_sources"]}; stream records {e["stream_records"]}; checker diagnostics {e["checker_diagnostics"]}.','',('Finished inside its bound.' if e['complete'] else 'Did not finish inside its bound. Totals cover emitted findings only. Unemitted findings are unknown, so these are not complete-program latent totals. No per-unit timing ledger was emitted.'),'',f'Ordinary census, 79 counted observations: NotYet {o["NotYet"]}, Refused {o["Refused"]}, panics {o["panic"]}, accepted {len(accepted)}. These are first-stop totals. The ordinary stream carries no latent counters, so ordinary full latent totals are unavailable.','','## Method, checkpoints and cleanup','','Read the 7910ab94 method and scripts first and reused its recipe at f1c19c6a. One adapted tree and an ordinary binary built from this SHA without an overlay. Sorted roots run sequentially in groups of 20, 20, 20 and 19. Each emits two observations (158 raw); only the first counts. run.py retains the prior per-root bounds and kills and reaps every child process group. Groups run directly in the foreground without the prior outer group timeout.','','Setup: source /workspace/adamic-tools/env.sh; bash cloud/setup.sh; npm ci --prefix stage3/api; export ADAMIC_TYPESCRIPT_SOURCE=/workspace/scratch/typescript-source. The source checkout HEAD is the pin above. apply-status.json and build-status.json identify the single apply and ordinary binary build.','','Guarded entry uses this SHA\'s stage3/census/latent/make_overlay.py and stage3/meter/entry_overlay.py, then go build with the resulting overlay. LATENT_ASSERT_NO_OUTPUT guards against usable IR output. Binary hashes, Go build metadata, adapted-source hashes and child status files identify measured bytes.','','A plain push to typescript/next-stops-f1c19c6a-checkpoint followed apply immediately, then each root group. checkpoint-push-*-status.json records each child exit. The final branch has one report-only commit directly on f1c19c6a. No force-push and no push to main.','','Every census child process group was killed and reaped, including after normal exits. validation.json records observation counts, duplicate agreement, source cleanliness and no surviving census processes. Files over 1 MB are gzip-compressed.']
text='\n'.join(lines)+'\n';assert '\u2014' not in text and '\u2013' not in text
(out/'REPORT.md').write_text(text)
